//! The threshold disease in the world (genetics specification 3.6, ADR-0019, ADR-0020
//! section 2, design note of the threshold disease): a person has it iff its liability `L`,
//! the phenotype of the trait named after the disease, lies above `T = probit(1 − K)`.
//!
//! The expected values come from `tools/state_reference.py` (scenario "threshold") and
//! `tools/liability_fixture.py`, which run the models of `tools/world_reference.py` and
//! `tools/data_reference.py`, written from the design note and not from this code.
//!
//! The data: the test map `tests/golden/data_liability`, the repository's map and life
//! course data plus the trait `core:disease_liability` with eight additive loci
//! `test:liability_1` to `_8` (effect 1, `d_ref` 1, `σ_ref` 2, so `G` runs from −4 to 4 in
//! steps of 1/2) and its phenotype row (`h²` 0.6, `c²` 0 in both ages); the threshold disease
//! names it. `K` = 0.01, so `T` = 2.32634787404084.
//!
//! Scenario "threshold": seed 0xff, founder tag `test:threshold5`, the switch on, three
//! couples (sims 1 and 2, 3 and 4, 5 and 8) at the start, no input after it, 12 years.
//! Sims 1, 2, 4, 6 and 7 carry the liability alleles twice (`G` 4), sim 3 once (`G` 0), sim
//! 5 twice at the first four loci and once at the last four (`G` 2), sim 8 none (`G` −4);
//! sim 7 also carries `core:disease_ad_late` once. Eight children are born (14 and 15
//! identical twins); sims 10 and 13 have the disease from birth. Sim 4 dies of it in year
//! 11, his onset before the start.

